// The controller's gRPC interface: what a client on another machine needs to
// see and steer the tasks that run here.
//
// It mirrors task.Backend one RPC per method. That is deliberate: a rule
// implemented in two places drifts, and the drift is what breaks. So the
// server side is the
// daemon's own file Store behind a switch, and the client side is a thin
// translation of the same interface - no second copy of the task model, and no
// second copy of the reconciliation, locking or liveness rules.
//
// Task records, events and live previews travel as the JSON the file backend
// already writes. Mirroring their fields here would be that second copy, and
// it would have to be edited in lockstep with the Go types for ever.

